   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The volume of water in a tank, in liters, is \\( V(t) = 4 t^{3} + 8 t + 8 \\) for time t in minutes. At what rate is the volume of water changing at the instant t = 5 minutes?",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 308
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "An average rate is available over any interval, so take the short interval from t = 5 to t = 5 + h. The average rate over it is \\( \\frac{V(5 + h) - V(5)}{h} \\).",
         "rule_named": "average rate of change over a short interval"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Expanding and dividing by h leaves \\( \\frac{V(5 + h) - V(5)}{h} = 4 h^{2} + 60 h + 308 \\), which still depends on the length h of the interval.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Multiply",
               4,
               [
                  "Power",
                  "h",
                  2
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               60,
               "h"
            ],
            308
         ],
         "rule_named": "difference quotient simplified"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The rate at the instant is what these averages approach as h approaches 0: \\( \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{V(5 + h) - V(5)}{h} = 308 \\). This limit is the derivative \\( V'(5) \\).",
         "mathjson": 308,
         "rule_named": "limit of the difference quotient"
      }
   ],
